WEBVTT

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.000
Hello, here we are again, ready

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.860
to go.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.920
Hope you have the easel set up and your almighty palette ready.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.350
We'll paint a fantastic little picture together.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.630
I'm gonna have them quickly run across the screen here,

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.860
all the colors that we have on the palette.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.420
So if you haven't caught those in one of the previous shows,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.970
you can pick up all the colors that we're using.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.710
I thought today we'd do a very quick, happy little waterfall.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.370
Last week, if you were with us, we did a waterfall

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.640
that was way off in the distance.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.420
This time I think we'll do one that's a little bit closer.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.570
So I'm gonna start today with a little tiny bit of phthalo blue

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.090
We'll mix a little Van Dyke brown with it.

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.350
And we'll just throw in a quick little sky here.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.280
Something about like so.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.120
And while I have the blue on the brush,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.620
I'll go right into a little bit of phthalo green,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.420
and we'll put some water in here,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:28.400
just to give us some nice little water indications.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.320
Okay.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.990
Now, let's wash the brush real quick.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.020
It'll move right along.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.060
Okay, now I'm gonna go into a tiny bit of alizarin crimson.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.300
Let's just warm this up a little.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.380
We'll put just a tiny bit of crimson right here.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.680
A little crimson.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.520
We don't want to set this guy on fire.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.440
Just want to give it a nice warm glow.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.540
A little bit into the water.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.670
Let's bring all this together.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.120
just using little criss-cross strokes back and forth,

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:11.730
sort of like you're making X's.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.370
Just very gently bring that together

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:21.090
so it's nice and evenly blended.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.990
Okay, let's take and put a,

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.550
let's put a little mountain way in the background.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.110
I use a little bit of Prussian blue,

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.600
Van Dyke brown, a touch of crimson.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.750
And we'll have a little mountain that's way back

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:43.550
in the distance back here, something like so.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.300
Just a little small one.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.410
Now with a large brush, I'm just gonna take

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:55.210
and pull that down so it blends it out on the bottom.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:59.350
I just want this mountain to literally just disappear.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:07.410
I'll take a little bit of white and I'm going to put

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.910
the least, least little amount of permanent red in it

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.720
just to put a little warm glow on the mountain.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.220
Tiny, tiny bit of permanent red.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.580
It's very, very strong.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:25.840
Okay, let's run a little highlight right down through here.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:27.230
I don't want these to be too bright.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.000
I want them to be far away, very soft.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:39.940
Maybe there's a little highlight striking right in here.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:44.490
This ridge.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.430
For the shadow side,

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:53.070
we'll take a little Prussian blue and white.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.120
Just drop some happy little shadows in here.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.880
Just let this one wander around and play here a little.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.800
Let your heart take you wherever you want to go.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.430
Maybe there's another little peak right there.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:21.580
Each highlight needs its own private shadow,

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:24.800
so just give him a shadow so he stands apart.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.900
Okay, with a clean, dry brush now,

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.400
I'm just gonna tap the bottom of this

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.260
just to create some mist.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:40.660
Over here, we'll follow these angles.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.890
Then lift upward.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:49.990
This one will be very soft, very far away.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:54.520
Okay, now let's take a little bit of Prussian blue,

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.680
Van Dyke brown, little tiny bit of sap green.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.000
We'll just mix it on the brush,

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.730
a little white with it.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.190
Let's make a happy little foothill

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.200
that comes running down here.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.800
There he is.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:17.240
Let's let him wander down here and have fun.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.860
All we're doing is tapping the canvas.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.700
Now you can take and lift gently upward

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.000
to make it look like little trees.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.960
Wee, wee, wee back in the distance there.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:35.790
Now then, maybe, let's do another one.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.300
That was a lot of fun.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.500
We'll take some blue and brown, sap green again.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.980
This one we'll want to be a little bit darker

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.400
because it's closer.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:51.130
We'll just have one run right down through here.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:56.280
Creates a lot of depth in your painting.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.910
We can just take the bottom of it and pull down

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.000
and create our reflection.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:21.710
Gently lift upward, make it look like little trees.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.290
Just make all kinds of little projections back here.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:28.500
Very gently, I'm gonna just wipe across

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.000
to turn it into reflections.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.650
Okay, we'll take a little bit of Magic White

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:38.620
and take a little waterline here.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.650
This is just straight Magic White.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:44.630
Remember our golden rule here, a thin paint

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.120
will stick to a thick paint.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:58.600
So this is very thin, so it'll stick right on there.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.000
Too bright.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.330
a little bit right out here.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.610
Now we could take a fan brush using the same dark colors,

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.040
blue, brown, a little sap green,

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.960
and we could just drop a few little indications

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.680
of trees back here.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:25.090
Maybe these are a little closer, just like so.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.690
Don't want to get too much detail yet.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.620
Let's darken this one up, it's closer.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.050
Then, with just a little tiny bit of yellow brush here,

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.330
I'm just gonna put a little highlight

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.310
so it looks like this is beginning to get close enough

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.320
that we can see things.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:53.310
Just here and there, very little.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.170
Okay, that gives us a nice background

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.970
for a little waterfall.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:08:00.000
Now, let's take the look

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.390
large brush, put some Prussian blue on it,

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:08.150
and a little Van Dyke brown.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:11.190
Here we need to figure out where the waterfall's gonna be.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.530
You have to make almighty decisions when you're the creator.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.540
And let's just say it's right here.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.920
Pull straight down.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.360
All we're doing is applying some dark

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.570
so our light color will show on top.

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:26.120
And let's throw some down in here.

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:43.020
Okay, clean the brush, we'll be ready to go here.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:47.190
And we'll use the fan brush and take a little tiny bit

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:52.780
of the Magic White and add to Firm White.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.260
Thin paint will stick to a thick paint,

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.180
so I've thinned it just a little bit here.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.600
We'll put some little ripples in the water.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.990
Just touch the canvas.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.480
Now, to make the waterfall,

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:16.570
pull the brush straight and let it fall.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:20.760
That's all there is to it, straight, fall.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.600
And it'll pay you to wipe the brush in between

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.610
because you're gonna pick up a little bit of that blue.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:33.510
Pull it over, let it fall.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.170
That's why they call 'em waterfalls.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.310
Okay, let's go over here.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:43.190
Pull it over, and let it fall.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:45.960
Over, and it falls.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.420
Type some of that blue off the brush,

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.560
and over, and fall.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:56.230
And that's how easy it is to make a little waterfall.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.590
Now, with a little more of the magic,

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.000
a little more titanium white,

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:03.050
we can begin letting it hit and splash

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:07.530
and have all kinds of little fun things happen down here.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:14.270
Now, we need to determine what's gonna contain this water.

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:17.220
So let's take Van Dyke Brown.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.480
Just straight Van Dyke Brown.

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:22.890
And we'll begin building some little cliffs and rocks.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.130
Something's gotta contain this.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:27.480
Be sure your rocks are higher than the waterfall.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.030
One thing that you have to remember,

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.300
Water is probably the laziest thing in nature.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.600
It will not climb a rock just so it can fall

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.200
and be pretty for you.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.720
It'd be nice if it would.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.970
It won't do it.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:47.940
Just fill this in with a lot of Van Dyke Brown.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:51.390
Over here, let's come right along like this.

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:54.390
Let this big old stone just play there.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:16.940
Just like so.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.630
I want to make these stones look flat on top.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:20.970
So I'll take a little burnt umber,

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.630
mix it with a Van Dyke brown.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.800
Maybe just a little touch of yellow into it.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.740
I want to try to make this look flat on top,

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:40.260
so this, when it comes across, needs to be like so.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:48.240
Keep it flat across here.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:56.430
Just let it go.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:58.450
And I burn umber, yellow.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:10.360
Let's have this one just sort of come around.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:14.610
Okay, angles.

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:20.540
Most important thing here, bring these angles down.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:23.500
A little bit of light color, just a tiny, tiny bit.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:25.450
Probably the biggest mistake made

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.270
is putting too much highlight under here.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:30.000
And you lose that beautiful darkness.

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:46.060
Just enough to create a little illusion of rocks here.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:48.480
You can do this like so every once in a while.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:56.830
Just to break it up a little.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:00.000
Angle so, most important.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.840
Now let's play with the water a little.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:11.930
Maybe it comes up in here and splashes and has fun.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.700
A little more of the magic white.

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:14.980
Be sure your paint's a little bit thinner

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:21.900
than what's on the canvas already.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.860
I'm having so much fun with rocks.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.580
I think I'll build another little happy stone

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:30.000
that comes right out through here.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:41.930
Van Dyke Brown, a little bit of our highlight color.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:52.270
Just let that work and play a little pull downward.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:58.800
Okay, let's take a little bit of the water over here.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.010
I'm going crazy with stones today.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:04.830
Let's just bring something down like that.

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:11.130
Maybe there's a big stone right here in the front.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.060
Remember, this is your world, so anywhere you want a stone,

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:19.680
that's where it should be.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:25.860
Just fill all that in.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.790
Creates a lot of depth by having all these different planes

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:29.600
in the painting.

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.840
and let's put a little bit of highlight out here

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:34.960
on this happy little stone.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:40.450
Just let that knife barely, barely touch, barely touch.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:46.210
It almost touches a canvas.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.420
We can just begin creating all kinds

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:51.910
of almighty stones and rocks.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.290
Okay, now, let's build,

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.630
let's build some happy little things here.

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:59.280
Use some Van Dyke Brown, some Burr Number mixed together.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.830
little bit of sap green in it.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.530
And let's just put, right over here,

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:08.410
just a happy little tree,

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:19.950
sittin' up here on this rock.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:24.140
Maybe over here, oh, there's an almighty tree.

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:26.220
That's where these big brushes really work beautiful,

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.620
so you wanna make big things.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:45.400
Man, you have to make decisions here.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.420
Where does it go?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.730
Where is the bottom of this tree?

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.790
Let's just let it run right on down here

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:55.550
and we'll decide that later.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.280
Let's put a few little Liam indications back here.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:05.940
just here and there, like that.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:10.420
And we'll highlight it with a little brown and white,

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.970
at least a little touch of blue,

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:19.320
just to put a little highlight on there.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.800
Okay, now we'll take some Magic White

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:24.140
to thin the paint a little bit.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:27.800
We'll go into a little bit of yellow,

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:29.060
a little bit of sap green.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.840
Yellow and sap green.

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:35.790
A lot of paint on the bristles.

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:39.530
And let's put some happy little leaves back in here.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:44.480
Just let these little leaves just fall off your brush.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:51.060
There's a little things happening.

00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:54.710
And go out sometime in the woods and study trees.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:57.420
Talk to trees, whatever it takes.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.890
Tree needs to be your friend if you're gonna paint him.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.010
Probably out in your yard, you have some beautiful trees

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.870
that you can look at.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:11.110
Study what happens in the tree.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:14.340
What makes each one an individual.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:19.080
Study nature.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:24.550
I really have some hang-ups about nature being destroyed.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:28.740
I would like to see nature remain the way it is.

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.000
I would like for my son

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:33.630
his grandchildren maybe, when he goes back to Alaska

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.510
to be able to see a real moose.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:37.620
Not just pictures of one.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:41.400
So appreciate what we have.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.850
Let's put a big ol' tree trunk right up through here.

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.640
This is just straight Van Dyke brown.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:04.600
Just fill that in real nice.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.740
And maybe there's a limb that just travels

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:10.370
right up through this way.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:16.330
You're a tree, so you put limbs where you want 'em.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:22.420
Okay, let's take a little bit of the titanium white,

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:26.400
with just a touch of umber in it, burnt umber.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.160
Let's just put some bark on like this today.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:47.770
Touch it, pull it to the side of the tree.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:51.650
Now, back to the magic white.

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:56.520
A little magic white, some yellow.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:58.670
And I want a darker color on this tree.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.000
So I'm gonna use a lot of sap

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:04.630
green on it, a lot of sap green.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:10.320
Want him to be darker than the one that's behind him.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:17.220
We can throw some happy little leaves right out here.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:25.420
Being darker, they stand apart a little better.

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:30.000
Yeah, let's make a happy little bush right out in here.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.750
Got some little brighter colors on him.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:41.530
So he stands out and shines.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.610
And on down here at the bottom

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:52.440
is all kind of little things growing out here on the stone.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.800
This one right here covers up half the tree's foots.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.700
This is a very nice little painting.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.380
It's a lot of fun to do.

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:06.540
It'll teach you a great deal.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.790
It's a good practice painting.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.270
It's also good for putting a happy buck

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:18.380
in your pocket once in a while.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.590
Maybe a little grassy thing over there somewhere.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:25.040
And you can also use the fan brush if you'd like.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.130
Just bring all this together very gently.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.850
There's a little weed that grows almost on the other side.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:41.900
Okay, with a palette knife, just a clean knife,

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:45.000
scrape a few little trunks and limbs in here.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.500
One of the important things when you're doing this

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.800
is don't kill all this dark hair, you really need it,

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:53.060
otherwise your painting will become very flat.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:59.320
You need the dark, it's the only way you can have light.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:09.080
Okay, let's go over here to the other side.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.890
I think that tree needs a little trunk.

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:20.160
Just touch, touch, touch Van Dyke brown.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.120
Highlight on it.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:27.160
This is brown and white.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.320
Just enough to give it some little indications.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:42.880
Let's highlight that tree, a little magic white,

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:54.710
a little yellow and sap green, right here on this one.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.640
And down here at the tree's bottom,

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:07.530
let's put a nice little bush right here.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:13.290
This is yellow ochre, beautiful color.

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:14.630
Maybe there's a little bush trying to live

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:17.100
down here on this stone.

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:20.160
Life can get rough down there.

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:24.760
Little sticks and twigs here and there.

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:27.430
But you're beginning to see now,

00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:30.000
how really very simple it is to do a happy little waterfall

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:36.450
It's no big secret, quite easy to do.

00:22:36.450 --> 00:22:41.610
I'm just throwing a few little sticks here and there.

00:22:41.610 --> 00:22:45.100
Okay, now we can take the fan brush,

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:47.920
little bit of magic white on it,

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:50.140
little bit of firm white.

00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:52.760
And now we can begin bringing the water all up through here.

00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:57.220
Just touch, bend the brush so it bends upward.

00:22:57.220 --> 00:23:00.000
Once again, it makes it look like

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:03.850
is dripping down, but you pull it upward,

00:23:03.850 --> 00:23:08.990
and do it in a real fast little motion.

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:10.390
Water's just going right on out,

00:23:10.390 --> 00:23:14.380
a little bubbly stream out from here.

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:19.880
Okay, now another thing that you can do,

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:22.370
just to make it look a little more finished,

00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:24.680
any time you have these big cliffs

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:26.720
with little things growing on it,

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:28.920
you always have a lot of little roots that hang over.

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:30.000
Just take your fan brush,

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.290
with a little tiny bit of color on it.

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:36.160
Pull, like so.

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:37.410
Just pull it.

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:40.380
Makes it look like little roots hanging over.

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:45.260
Isn't that something?

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:51.420
Just here and there.

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:53.790
Brush off.

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:56.170
Maybe we'll take the liner brush,

00:23:56.170 --> 00:24:00.000
a little Van Dyke Brown, and we'll put

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.870
a couple little stems and stuff up through here.

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:05.850
Maybe there's a little limb that comes

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:09.130
right up through here like so.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:10.710
This is just a thin oil.

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:14.870
Just about any type of oil will work.

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:16.330
Just thins the paint down a little bit.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:18.800
You may thin it with paint thinner if you desire.

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:21.400
Be careful because paint thinner will bleed,

00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:23.820
like ink on rice paper.

00:24:23.820 --> 00:24:27.300
Be very careful with that.

00:24:27.300 --> 00:24:30.000
The oil is slick, it moves much easier.

00:24:35.150 --> 00:24:36.430
across the front.

00:24:36.430 --> 00:24:37.730
When you're doing little trees and stuff,

00:24:37.730 --> 00:24:40.150
one thing to avoid, don't have a trunk

00:24:40.150 --> 00:24:42.780
and then limbs coming just off each side,

00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:44.820
because some of the limbs are in front of the trunk,

00:24:44.820 --> 00:24:51.570
some are in the back, so have them come across.

00:24:51.570 --> 00:24:55.880
That just gives us a little something right there.

00:24:55.880 --> 00:24:57.160
A few little sticks and twigs,

00:24:57.160 --> 00:24:58.640
just little finishing touches.

00:25:01.470 --> 00:25:04.300
I think I'm beginning to piddle right now.

00:25:04.300 --> 00:25:06.540
So I'm gonna take a little bit of the oil,

00:25:06.540 --> 00:25:08.670
a little permanent red.

00:25:08.670 --> 00:25:09.870
I think it's time we signed this one

00:25:09.870 --> 00:25:13.300
and called it finished.

00:25:13.300 --> 00:25:16.180
Okay, work your oil in there to your paint.

00:25:16.180 --> 00:25:17.700
It's just like water.

00:25:17.700 --> 00:25:22.190
And turn the brush to bring it back to a nice sharp point.

00:25:22.190 --> 00:25:28.960
Okay, let's go right along in here.

00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:30.000
When you have this oil very thin,

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:35.780
thin like this, it's just about like writing with a pen.

00:25:35.780 --> 00:25:37.860
Another way you can sign your name is just take the back

00:25:37.860 --> 00:25:39.760
of your liner brush and you can scrape right through

00:25:39.760 --> 00:25:45.990
the paint, your signature will be there.

00:25:45.990 --> 00:25:50.820
Okay, I think we just about have a finished painting here.

00:25:50.820 --> 00:25:54.810
Now this is a very, very fun little painting to do.

00:25:54.810 --> 00:25:58.010
It teaches you a great deal and I hope it helps you.

00:25:58.010 --> 00:26:00.000
If you've enjoyed this, you know,

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.320
Let your PBS station know.

00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:03.450
That's the only way we know what you like.

00:26:03.450 --> 00:26:05.530
Let us hear from you once in a while.

00:26:05.530 --> 00:26:08.530
So on behalf of all of us here at this station,

00:26:08.530 --> 00:26:09.990
we'd like to wish you happy painting,

00:26:09.990 --> 00:26:12.680
and we're looking forward to seeing you again next week.

00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:16.580
Until then, have a super day.
